                    {
                        "sense_id": "b65e9631-0cc3-371e-bbbe-384726a48a6a",
                        "entry_id": "3614f5ad-b3cf-33ad-a1e6-26972f4e3625",
                        "glosses": [
                            "книжн. художественная манера максимально утончённых и изысканных изображений"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "d3ad982f-70e2-395a-b014-9bfc1c67a9a3",
                        "entry_id": "3614f5ad-b3cf-33ad-a1e6-26972f4e3625",
                        "glosses": [
                            "книжн. чрезмерное увлечение внешними формами в искусстве в ущерб идейной стороне произведения"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "f970a4ce-2a99-4930-a434-7521bf5a37ca",
                                "sense_id": "d3ad982f-70e2-395a-b014-9bfc1c67a9a3",
                                "text": "Два структурных рисунка разные: у Леонтьева красота как оболочка, внешний продольный слой бытия, у Флоренского — сила, пронизывающая все слои поперек. Флоренский изобразил даже схему-чертёж строения этих двух эстетизмов."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "bdd412f0-0333-445c-b3c4-d43ab6aa9935",
                        "source_entry_id": "3614f5ad-b3cf-33ad-a1e6-26972f4e3625",
                        "target_lang_word": "aestheticism",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "aestheticism",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "cce9e1e2-d434-3302-9d72-7140c03c07c8",
                                        "entry_id": "e1039116-9f35-3eaf-afa8-105f4f4057c8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A doctrine which holds aesthetics or beauty as the highest ideal or most basic standard."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e4b4fb1c-34ff-490d-9793-2a14d0017f8c",
                                                "sense_id": "cce9e1e2-d434-3302-9d72-7140c03c07c8",
                                                "text": "He went over his canvases with disgust and anger, unable to see virtue in any one of them. Even his sacred Oyster Girl went back on him. The creature of a vitiated æstheticism, he could only suppose that conceit had played an abominable trick on his eyesight."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e4426527-1ef6-4bbd-b122-2b20b7f74e7a",
                                                "sense_id": "cce9e1e2-d434-3302-9d72-7140c03c07c8",
                                                "text": "Born the most sensitive of children into an unhappy family that misreared and misschooled him, Rilke recoiled into introspectiveness and dilletante^([sic]) aestheticism, and long remained there; the world, or outwardness, was what had hurt him, was the enemy."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
